From f54994f6c797803ef389ae863a06ca8dca2592a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Ottenhoff <AlexanderOttenhoff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:47:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Android: native window, RGBA8 presentation, boundless
 texture cache set

- Application window: SDL display bounds, a fullscreen window and the
  ANativeWindow handle from SDL_SysWMinfo.
- Present RGBA8 on Android, the only format Android surfaces guarantee.
- Texture cache descriptor arrays of 1024 on Android
  (RT64_TEXTURE_CACHE_SIZE), keeping the set boundless
  (update-after-bind, partially bound, variable count); Adreno lost the
  device when those flags were dropped.
- Integer-scale resolution rounds down on Android.

Everything is behind __ANDROID__ / if (ANDROID). Tested on a Retroid
Pocket 6 (Adreno 740).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ed54bfeefc5674fe572b71867822edbd13826c57)
---
 CMakeLists.txt                      |  3 +++
 src/hle/rt64_application.cpp        |  5 ++++
 src/hle/rt64_application_window.cpp | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/hle/rt64_workload_queue.cpp     |  4 ++++
 src/render/rt64_descriptor_sets.h   | 12 ++++++++++
 src/render/rt64_shader_library.cpp  |  5 ++++
